# prev/at (and question words) in binding position — F-OURO-18 re-land
# (ouroboros#57 item 3). prev/at bind with `is` and compound ops, serve as
# params / loop vars, and their special forms still win. At the pinned
# runtime the identifier FALLBACK takes no postfix (`prev[0]` splits into
# `prev` + a discarded `[0]` statement — upstream #328 changes this on
# main, unreleased).
prev is [1, 2]
print of prev
at is 3
at += 2
print of at
define scale(prev) as:
    return prev * 2
print of (scale of 6)
total is 0
for what in [1, 2, 3]:
    total is total + what
print of total
# special form still wins: `prev of x` is temporal
x is 1
x is 5
print of (prev of x)
# fallback takes no postfix: `[0]` below is a separate, discarded statement
p2 is prev
[0]
print of p2[0]
